The operator approved this split in the architect REPL (2026-10-27).

R10 cannot be planned whole yet, for two reasons:
- its "owned attempt workspaces" are R09's guest materialization contract, and R09 is BLOCKED with no plan;
- it spans five concerns, so it would exceed the size cap.

New R10a (task-7988e5b97ea0484fae6bf8e49009266a, PLANNING, dependsOn R08) takes item 1 of R08's handoff: signal-safe guest job teardown in guest-supervisor.py relay().
- SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGINT kill and reap the job's session group, with a new fixed exit code.
- A SIGKILL of the supervisor still ends the job's session.
R10a is file-disjoint from R09, and R08 has landed code (b0e5982).

This row stays the final slice and keeps its full DoD. It now dependsOn R09 and R10a, and still R08 indirectly through R10a. Plan it once both have landed code. It still owns:
- the job table that replaces main()'s EX_CONFIG;
- running the agent as moe-agent (R07 already makes that identity with no sudo or groups);
- scoped provider credentials;
- fresh session identity, so that full context is forced;
- artifact preservation, and lease release on exit or crash;
- host-side kill-and-verify termination evidence in guest-session.mjs (R08 handoff item 2).
Expect a further SPIDR split at that point (job table and identity; credentials; reconnect). The R09 final plan defines the workspace layout this row consumes.
